    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:d1bf136a4a3c936a",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "d36949198189bc2e32810ce75e4d7f399ee00668a20a7d52f6d9da395b1db19a",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261107-mw6m8vuu",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, set out on a tour of Tierra del Fuego National Park lasting about **4 hours**.\n\nThe park covers approximately **63,000 hectares** and has about **6 km** of coastline along the Beagle Channel. It is one of the world's southernmost nature reserves.\n\nOver the course of the tour, you will see rocky mountains, valleys, rivers and blue lakes. The walk follows the Pipo River, with views of Mount Susana, Redonda Island, Ensenada Bay and Lake Roca.\n\n**Helicopter flight over Ushuaia**\n\nAn optional helicopter flight of about **10 minutes** is available over Ushuaia or Drake Bay."
    },
